ized** |\n37: > | **Data Source** | NexLev API (fresh data) |\n38: > | **Timestamp** | August 30, 2026 |\n39: \n40: **21.8K subs + 29.7M views = NOT MONETIZED.** This is a critical finding.\n41: \n42: ### Why Nemo might not be monetized:\n43: \n44: 1. **COPPA / Made for Kids** — If the channel is flagged as kids content, YouTube may have restricted monetization\n45: 2. **Reused Content Policy** — YouTube's \"repetitious content\" policy targets channels where videos are too similar to each other (Nemo's thumbnails/titles are nearly identical)\n46: 3. **Didn't apply** — The creator may not have applied for YPP (YouTube Partner Program) yet\n47: 4. **Country restrictions** — If the creator is in a country where YPP is limited\n48: 5. **Community Guidelines strikes** — Past violations could block monetization\n49: \n50: > [!WARNING]\n51: > **This is a HUGE risk signal for the GTA kids niche.** MARINARA is monetized and making $74K/month, but Nemo with similar content and 29.7M views is NOT monetized. YouTube may be selectively enforcing content policies in this space.\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## 3. RPM & Revenue Estimate\n56: \n57: > **Note**: `get_geography_revenue` was rate-limited (5/5 daily calls used). Using MARINARA's niche data as reference since both channels are in the same GTA Spider-Man niche.\n58: \n59: | Metric | MARINARA (reference) | **Nemo (estimated)** |\n60: |--------|---------------------|---------------------|\n61: | Category RPM | $2.30 | ~$2.30 (same niche) |\n62: | Channel RPM | $1.98 | **$0.00** ❌ |\n63: | Monthly Revenue | $74,948 | **$0.00** ❌ |\n64: | Total Lifetime Earnings | ~$161K | **$0.00** ❌ |\n65: \n66: > [!IMPORTANT]\n67: > **29.7 MILLION views and ZERO dollars earned.** If Nemo were monetized at MARINARA's RPM ($1.98), they would have earned approximately **$58,756 lifetime**. Instead: nothing. This is the risk of the GTA kids niche — YouTube can decide you don't qualify.\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 4. Nemo vs MARINARA — Same Niche