dge (school level) | $0 | |\n| **Total startup cost** | **$0** | |\n\n**Realistic first-year earnings**: $15,000-30,000 if you post 2-3 videos/week\n\n### If you can research tech topics → **Tech Explainers (Byte Sized Style)**\n\n| What You Need | Cost | Time to First \\$ |\n|---------------|------|------------------|\n| Canva (free tier) | $0 | ~3-4 months |\n| TTS voice | $0 | |\n| Icon/image libraries | $0 | |\n| Strong research skills | $0 | |\n| **Total startup cost** | **$0** | |\n\n**Realistic first-year earnings**: $20,000-50,000 if you nail the format (2 videos/month)\n\n### DO NOT START: GTA Kids Content\n\nDespite MARINARA's $74K/month, **Nemo proves this niche can pay $0 for the same work.** YouTube's COPPA and repetitious content policies make this a lottery ticket, not a business.\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ The Bottom Line\n\n| | Math Education | Tech Explainer |\n|--|---------------|----------------|\n| **Easiest to start** | ✅ Yes | Close second |\n| **Highest RPM** | ❌ $1.72 | ✅ $5.80 |\n| **Best revenue/video** | ❌ $161 | ✅ $4,678 |\n| **Safest (lowest risk)** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |\n| **Fastest to monetize** | ✅ Evergreen search | ⚠️ Needs viral hits |\n| **Best long-term** | Good | **Best** |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **If I had to pick ONE**: Start with **Tech Explainers (Byte Sized style)**. It's nearly as easy as math, pays 3.4x higher RPM ($5.80 vs $1.72), and earns $4,678 per video vs $161. The \"Every ___ Explained\" format with TTS voice and icon grids is the best risk-adjusted return of all 10 channels analyzed.\n>\n> **If you know math well**: Start with **Math Education** — it's the absolute lowest barrier to entry. $0 cost, 2-4 hours per video, and Brain Station proves you can reach 460K subs with simple whiteboard animations. Then expand to tech later.\n\n---\n\n## Data Sources — All NexLev, All Real\n\n| Channel | `youtube_channel_about` | `get_geography_revenue` | `check_channel_monetization` |\n|---------|------------------------|----------------------