oad Frequency** | ~5 per week | N/A | — | vidIQ-only metric |\n| **Views Gained (7D)** | +1,491,132 | N/A | — | vidIQ-only metric |\n| **Views Gained (30D)** | +3,670,779 | 3,393,641 (monthly views) | ⚠️ Close | Different measurement windows |\n| **Sub Growth %** | +210.47% | N/A | — | vidIQ-only metric |\n| **Monetized** | ✅ Yes (badge) | N/A (not checked) | — | vidIQ shows monetization badge |\n| **Channel Rank (subs)** | #821K | N/A | — | vidIQ-only metric |\n| **Category Rank** | #270K (Lifestyle) | N/A | — | vidIQ-only metric |\n| **RPM** | Not shown | **\\$1.69** | — | **NexLev-only metric** |\n| **Tier 1 Traffic %** | Not shown | **75.2%** | — | **NexLev-only metric** |\n| **Demographics** | Not shown | Full gender/age/geo | — | **NexLev-only metric** |\n\n### Key Differences Explained\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> ### vidIQ says \\$9.9K/month. NexLev says \\$5.6K/month. Which is right?\n>\n> **NexLev is more accurate.** Here's why:\n>\n> - **vidIQ** estimates revenue using the **category average RPM** without accounting for geographic distribution. It sees \"Lifestyle\" category (their classification) and applies a generic RPM.\n> - **NexLev** calculates revenue using the **actual channel RPM** (\\$1.69) which factors in the 24.8% India traffic that drags down CPMs.\n> - The math confirms NexLev: 3,393,641 views × \\$1.69/1000 = ~\\$5,735 (close to NexLev's \\$5,594)\n> - **vidIQ overestimates by ~77%** for this channel specifically because of the high India traffic percentage.\n\n### What vidIQ Does Better\n| vidIQ Advantage | Detail |\n|----------------|--------|\n| **Growth metrics** | Views gained 7D/30D, sub growth % — shows momentum |\n| **VPH (Views Per Hour)** | Shows which videos are currently viral |\n| **Breakout score** | 15.9x on Intelligence video — identifies outliers |\n| **Similar channels** | Thinkplicit (12K), Stratagem (3,190), Why You Do That (5,660) |\n| **Upload frequency** | ~5 per week — NexLev doesn't calculate this |\n| **Monetization badge** | Quick visual confirmation |\n\n### What NexLev Does Better\n| NexLev Advantage | Detail |\n|-----------------|--------|\n| **Actual RPM** | \\$1.69 channel RPM vs vidIQ's category-based guess |\n| **Revenue accuracy** | \\$5,594 vs vidIQ's inflated \\$9,900 |\n| **Demographics** | Full gender/age/country breakdown |\n| **Geographic revenue impact** | Shows exactly why RPM is low (24.8% India) |\n| **Channel type** | LONG_ONLY classification |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Similar Channels (From vidIQ)\n\n| Channel | Subscribers | Content Type |\n|---------|------------|-------------|\n| **Thinkplicit** | 12K | Psychology/self-improvement animations |\n| **Stratagem** | 3,190 | Psychology/strategy animations |\n| **Why You Do That** | 5,660 | Behavioral psychology explainers |\n\n> PsychToons is the **clear leader** in this micro-niche — 81.3K subs vs the next competitor at just 12K. The niche has very low competition.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Key Insights\n\n### 🚀 Growth Trajectory — One of the Fastest Growing Channels We've Analyzed\n- **Sub growth: +210%** in recent period (vidIQ)\n- **Current monthly views (3.4M)** represent **53% of ALL lifetime views** (6.4M) — most of the channel's success is from the last 30 days\n- **Current revenue (\\$5,594) is 2.83x the lifetime average** (\\$1,974)\n- At this trajectory, the channel could reach **200K+ subs** and **\\$10K+/month** within 3-4 months\n\n### 🎨 Content Format — Animated Psychology Explainers\n- **Custom animations** with illustrated characters\n- **Psychology topic + provocative title hook**: \"Learn Anything So Fast It's Almost Unfair\", \"Be So Productive It Feels Illegal\"\n- **~15 minute videos** — long enough for mid-roll ads\n- **~5 uploads per week** — extremely aggressive upload pace\n- **No face, no voice recording** — likely TTS or hired voiceover\n\n### 💰 RPM Reality\n- \\$1.69 RPM is **LOW** for the content quality\n- The 24.8% India traffic is the main drag\n- If the channel shifted its audience to 50%+ US (currently 32.5%), RPM could jump to \\$2.50+\n- **Psychology pays less than Tech** (\\$1.69 vs \\$5.80) but gets more viral views\n\n### 📊 Difficulty to Replicate: ⭐⭐⭐⭐ HARD\nUnlike stickman animations or math whiteboard videos:\n- Needs **custom illustration** for every video (not templates)\n- Needs **animation skills** or hiring an animator\n- Needs **good psychology research** and scriptwriting\n- The visual quality bar is HIGH — can't do this in PowerPoint\n- **This is NOT an easy niche to enter** despite being faceless\n\n---\n\n## 9. PsychToons vs All Previously Analyzed Channels\n\n| Metric | Brain Station | Byte Sized | Cineporty | StickmanTeck | Stickman 616 | Vericade | MARINARA | Rock in Space | **PsychToons** |\n|--------|-------------|-----------|-----------|-------------|-------------|---------|---------|-------------|--------------|\n| **Niche** | Math | Tech | Horror | Tech | MCU | MCU | GTA Kids | Myths | **Psychology** |\n| **Subs** | 460K | 183K | 12K | 5.16K | 21.1K | 71.7K | 109K | 337K | **81.3K** |\n| **Videos** | 319 | 24 | 15 | 20 | 32 | 307 | 162 | 15 | **110** |\n| **Total Views** | 29.9M | 19.4M | 4.04M | 538K | 8.51M | 78.2M | 81.3M | 26.2M | **6.4M** |\n| **Long RPM** | \\$1.72 | \\$5.80 | \\$2.52 | \\$5.90 | \\$2.57 | \\$5.18 | \\$1.98 | \\$3.24 | **\\$1.69** |\n| **Monthly Rev** | \\$3,065 | \\$8,150 | \\$3,323 | \\$1,681 | \\$8,636 | \\$548 | \\$74,948 | \\$4,887 | **\\$5,594** |\n| **Lifetime** | ~\\$51K | ~\\$112K | ~\\$10K | ~\\$3.2K | ~\\$21.9K | ~\\$30.5K | ~\\$161K | ~\\$85K | **~\\$10.9K** |\n| **Rev/Video** | \\$161 | **\\$4,678** | \\$221 | \\$84 | \\$270 | \\$1.79 | \\$463 | **\\$5,671** | **\\$98.68** |\n| **Views/Video** | 93.6K | 807K | 269K | 27K | 266K | 255K | 502K | 1.75M | **58.3K** |\n| **Per Year** | \\$37K | \\$98K | \\$40K | \\$20K | \\$104K | \\$6.6K | \\$900K | \\$59K | **\\$67K** |\n| **Tier 1 %** | 70.3% | 72.3% | 81.6% | 76.3% | 80.2% | 81.5% | 77.2% | 67.4% | **75.2%** |\n| **Growth** |